IMPORT `wpa-types`
IMPORT `wpa-deductions`
IMPORT `wpa-payment`
IMPORT `wpa-enforcement`
IMPORT `wpa-goal`

-- Wages Protection Act 1983 — TESTS.
-- Expected values are worked from ../source/WPA1983.txt, not from the code.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

`consent` MEANS `the worker's written consent` FALSE FALSE
`general clause` MEANS `the worker's written consent` TRUE FALSE
`consent by duress` MEANS `the worker's written consent` FALSE TRUE

-- A deduction: amount, date, basis; for a lawful purpose, consulted, not
-- unreasonable, never withdrawn.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, b IS A `Basis for the deduction`
GIVETH A Deduction
`deduct` amount `on` d `under` b MEANS Deduction OF amount, d, b, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, b IS A `Basis for the deduction`, purpose IS A BOOLEAN, consulted IS A BOOLEAN, unreasonable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Deduction
`deduct` amount `on` d `under` b `, lawful purpose` purpose `, consulted` consulted `, unreasonable` unreasonable MEANS
    Deduction OF amount, d, b, purpose, consulted, unreasonable, NOTHING

`notice of 1 March 2025` MEANS `Notice of withdrawal` OF Date 1 3 2025, TRUE, Date 1 3 2025
`impracticable notice of 1 March 2025` MEANS `Notice of withdrawal` OF Date 1 3 2025, FALSE, Date 10 4 2025

-- The overpayment: $500, the worker absent without authority, not a
-- specified pay deduction, not avoidable, paid 1 July 2025, next pay day
-- 8 July 2025, recovered 15 July 2025, notice given on the day stated.
GIVEN w IS A `Workplace of the worker`, `the notice day` IS A DATE, `the recovery day` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN Overpayment
`overpayment` w `notice on` `the notice day` `recovered` `the recovery day` MEANS
    Overpayment OF 500, `(a) absent from work without the employer's authority`, FALSE, TRUE, Date 1 7 2025, Date 8 7 2025, w,
                   JUST (`Overpayment notice` OF `the notice day`, TRUE, TRUE, 0, FALSE), `the recovery day`

`a good overpayment` MEANS `overpayment` `(iv) any other case` `notice on` (Date 8 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 15 7 2025)

GIVEN m IS A `Manner of payment`, crown IS A BOOLEAN, consent IS A BOOLEAN, absent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment facts`
`paid by` m `, Crown:` crown `, consent:` consent `, absent:` absent MEANS
    `Payment facts` OF m, 900, Date 30 6 2026, crown, consent, NOTHING, absent, FALSE, FALSE

§§ `Goal 1 — dates`

#ASSERT `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` (Date 1 4 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` (Date 31 3 2016)

-- ss 5(2), 9(2): within 2 weeks if practicable, else as soon as practicable
-- Changed 2026-10-17 (Legislation Act s 55, applied at the user's direction): the 2 weeks from 1 March 2025 end on Saturday 15 March, so the employer may act on the old consent to Monday 17 March; the last day is 17 March.
#ASSERT `the last day the employer may act on the old consent, after` `notice of 1 March 2025` EQUALS Date 17 3 2025
#ASSERT `the consent or request still covers what is done on` (Date 15 3 2025) `, notice` (JUST `notice of 1 March 2025`)
-- Changed 2026-10-17 (Legislation Act s 55, applied at the user's direction): the 2 weeks from 1 March 2025 end on Saturday 15 March, so the employer may act on the old consent to Monday 17 March; 16 March is still covered.
#ASSERT `the consent or request still covers what is done on` (Date 16 3 2025) `, notice` (JUST `notice of 1 March 2025`)
#ASSERT `the consent or request still covers what is done on` (Date 10 4 2025) `, notice` (JUST `impracticable notice of 1 March 2025`)
#ASSERT NOT `the consent or request still covers what is done on` (Date 11 4 2025) `, notice` (JUST `impracticable notice of 1 March 2025`)
#ASSERT `the consent or request still covers what is done on` (Date 1 1 2030) `, notice` NOTHING

§§ `Goal 1 — overpayments (s 6)`

#ASSERT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` `a good overpayment`
-- s 6(1): no recoverable period
#ASSERT NOT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (Overpayment OF 500, `none of these`, FALSE, TRUE, Date 1 7 2025, Date 8 7 2025, `(iv) any other case`, JUST (`Overpayment notice` OF Date 8 7 2025, TRUE, TRUE, 0, FALSE), Date 15 7 2025)
#ASSERT `an overpayment within s 6(1)` (Overpayment OF 500, `(b) on strike`, FALSE, TRUE, Date 1 7 2025, Date 8 7 2025, `(iv) any other case`, NOTHING, Date 15 7 2025)
#ASSERT `an overpayment within s 6(1)` (Overpayment OF 500, `(d) suspended`, FALSE, TRUE, Date 1 7 2025, Date 8 7 2025, `(iv) any other case`, NOTHING, Date 15 7 2025)
-- s 6(3)(a): avoidable
#ASSERT NOT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (Overpayment OF 500, `(a) absent from work without the employer's authority`, FALSE, FALSE, Date 1 7 2025, Date 8 7 2025, `(iv) any other case`, JUST (`Overpayment notice` OF Date 8 7 2025, TRUE, TRUE, 0, FALSE), Date 15 7 2025)
-- s 6(3)(b): no notice
#ASSERT NOT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (Overpayment OF 500, `(a) absent from work without the employer's authority`, FALSE, TRUE, Date 1 7 2025, Date 8 7 2025, `(iv) any other case`, NOTHING, Date 15 7 2025)
-- s 6(3)(c)(iv): not later than the next pay day (8 July)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (`overpayment` `(iv) any other case` `notice on` (Date 9 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 15 7 2025))
-- (c)(i): not later than 10 days after the next pay day (18 July)
#ASSERT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (`overpayment` `(i) no fixed workplace` `notice on` (Date 18 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 20 7 2025))
#ASSERT NOT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (`overpayment` `(i) no fixed workplace` `notice on` (Date 19 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 20 7 2025))
-- (c)(ii), (iii): not later than the first day the worker attends after the next pay day
#ASSERT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (`overpayment` (`(ii) one fixed workplace, not attended during normal hours on the next pay day` (Date 14 7 2025)) `notice on` (Date 14 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 20 7 2025))
#ASSERT NOT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (`overpayment` (`(ii) one fixed workplace, not attended during normal hours on the next pay day` (Date 14 7 2025)) `notice on` (Date 15 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 20 7 2025))
#ASSERT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (`overpayment` (`(iii) 2 or more fixed workplaces, none attended during normal hours on the next pay day` (Date 21 7 2025)) `notice on` (Date 21 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 25 7 2025))
-- (b) "before recovering": recovery before the notice fails; the same day passes (FORK F2)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (`overpayment` `(iv) any other case` `notice on` (Date 8 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 7 7 2025))
#ASSERT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (`overpayment` `(iv) any other case` `notice on` (Date 8 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 8 7 2025))
-- (d): recovered not later than 2 months after the notice (8 September)
#ASSERT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (`overpayment` `(iv) any other case` `notice on` (Date 8 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 8 9 2025))
#ASSERT NOT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (`overpayment` `(iv) any other case` `notice on` (Date 8 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 9 9 2025))
-- s 6(4)(a): the notice need not state the amount if it gives the day and the actions
#ASSERT `the notice identifies the overpayment` (`Overpayment notice` OF Date 8 7 2025, FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the notice identifies the overpayment` (`Overpayment notice` OF Date 8 7 2025, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE)
-- (ba): a specified pay deduction — 10 working days, and the s 95C method
#ASSERT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (Overpayment OF 500, `(b) on strike`, TRUE, TRUE, Date 1 7 2025, Date 8 7 2025, `(iv) any other case`, JUST (`Overpayment notice` OF Date 15 7 2025, TRUE, TRUE, 10, TRUE), Date 20 7 2025)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (Overpayment OF 500, `(b) on strike`, TRUE, TRUE, Date 1 7 2025, Date 8 7 2025, `(iv) any other case`, JUST (`Overpayment notice` OF Date 16 7 2025, TRUE, TRUE, 11, TRUE), Date 20 7 2025)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` (Overpayment OF 500, `(b) on strike`, TRUE, TRUE, Date 1 7 2025, Date 8 7 2025, `(iv) any other case`, JUST (`Overpayment notice` OF Date 15 7 2025, TRUE, TRUE, 10, FALSE), Date 20 7 2025)

§§ `Goal 1 — deductions (ss 4, 5, 5A, 15, 16)`

`a day in 2026` MEANS Date 30 6 2026

#ASSERT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` `a day in 2026` `under` `consent`)
#ASSERT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` `a day in 2026` `under` (`the worker's written request` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` `a day in 2026` `under` `no written consent or request`)
-- s 5(1A): a general deductions clause needs consultation first
#ASSERT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` `a day in 2026` `under` `general clause` `, lawful purpose` TRUE `, consulted` TRUE `, unreasonable` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` `a day in 2026` `under` `general clause` `, lawful purpose` TRUE `, consulted` FALSE `, unreasonable` FALSE)
-- consultation matters only for a general deductions clause
#ASSERT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` `a day in 2026` `under` `consent` `, lawful purpose` TRUE `, consulted` FALSE `, unreasonable` FALSE)
-- s 5A
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` `a day in 2026` `under` `consent` `, lawful purpose` TRUE `, consulted` TRUE `, unreasonable` TRUE)
-- s 5(1) "for a lawful purpose"
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` `a day in 2026` `under` `consent` `, lawful purpose` FALSE `, consulted` TRUE `, unreasonable` FALSE)
-- duress
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` `a day in 2026` `under` `consent by duress`)
-- ss 15, 16
#ASSERT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` `a day in 2026` `under` `required or authorised by another Act (s 15)`)
#ASSERT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` `a day in 2026` `under` `a collective agreement or an order of the Court or Authority (s 16)`)
-- s 6(2)
#ASSERT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 500 `on` (Date 15 7 2025) `under` (`recovery of an overpayment under s 6` `a good overpayment`))
#ASSERT NOT `the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 500 `on` (Date 15 7 2025) `under` (`recovery of an overpayment under s 6` (`overpayment` `(iv) any other case` `notice on` (Date 9 7 2025) `recovered` (Date 15 7 2025))))
-- s 5(2): after the withdrawal day
#ASSERT `the deduction was lawful` (Deduction OF 50, Date 15 3 2025, `consent`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, JUST `notice of 1 March 2025`)
-- Changed 2026-10-17 (Legislation Act s 55, applied at the user's direction): the 2 weeks from 1 March 2025 end on Saturday 15 March, so the employer may act on the old consent to Monday 17 March; a deduction on 16 March is lawful.
#ASSERT `the deduction was lawful` (Deduction OF 50, Date 16 3 2025, `consent`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, JUST `notice of 1 March 2025`)
-- before 1 April 2016
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the deduction was lawful` (`deduct` 50 `on` (Date 1 3 2016) `under` `consent`))

